  "notes": "737-700 ICAO type B737. Drawn from the 2022 photo of N955WN (left side, from below; the 2025 photos show the same scheme). The flag's 13 rays fan from the star up over the crown and aft; the four clearest yellow rays are drawn on red, the rest are hidden by the angle. Rays over the crown are continued straight from the star. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the fin is the state jets' Heart fin as re-measured on Colorado One (the same fin on every 737), copied with its title and flag. 'Arizona One' measured on the 2022 photo against the nose and the forward door (x 0.065-0.10 of the 737-700), two weights, a pair of titles per side, on Colorado One's line under the cockpit windows (it had been placed above them). The yellow field's curved upper edge made smooth. Drawn on the 737-700 (no measured shape for it)."
